WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.710
Arguably, one of the most important skills of this era in AI is creating skills for AI.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.510
But a weak skill runs at the wrong moment, or stays silent when you need it.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.210
It's like a colleague who speaks up in every meeting,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.870
and disappears the day you need help.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.530
That's because the task was a poor fit, or the AI guessed how you work.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:30.470
And while any AI tool can help you craft a skill, not every skill is as useful.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:40.070
And knowing what a good skill looks like, when to build one and how to improve it will radically improve the results you get from your AI tools.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:49.630
So in this adventure, you check whether your task deserves a skill, build it with one prompt that interviews you, and test it on real work.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.450
That prompt then builds every skill from here on.
